         <change when="2026-03-25T07:20:38-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - I've tacitly restored the eta in lin4 (κη̣ρωματικ(οῦ)), which was the original reading in PSI 7 805 (κ̣η̣ρωματικ ), cf. e.g. the one in Ἑρμῆς in lin7. The left vertical leg is characteristic. The papyrus was subsequently re-edited by R. Bagnall (Studia Papyrologica 1982), where the word was printed as κερωματικ(οῦ), without dots. Then, this was reprinted in SB 16. I don't consider it a correction but perhaps a misprint. </change>
